# The service surface every docs-site sample is allowed to assume (M62, DT-04).
#
# `scripts/verify-docs.mjs` drops each ```tflw sample into a scratch directory next to this file
# and checks it with the shipped CLI. A sample naming a service that isn't declared here fails with
# `TF026` — which is the point: this list is a conscious decision about what the documentation may
# reference without introducing it, not a wildcard that makes the check pass.
#
# The URLs are deliberately unroutable. Nothing here ever runs: `tflw check` parses and validates,
# it never opens a socket. A reachable host would invite a sample that quietly depends on one.
#
# Sessions live in `sessions.config` next door rather than here, because a ```tflw-config fragment
# sample is completed with *this* file — and several of those samples declare a session themselves,
# which against a fixture that already declared it is `TF029`, a duplicate name.

env docs default
  api "http://127.0.0.1:9"
  web "http://127.0.0.1:9"

  # M128b — the docs may document `expect response has no … security violations` (guide chapter 14),
  # and writing that assertion without a matching declaration is `TF060`. Declared here for the same
  # reason the services above are: the fixture states what a sample is allowed to assume, and a
  # sample teaching a security assertion has to be able to compile. The origin matches `api` exactly,
  # since `TF060` compares origins and this one is deliberately unroutable.
  authorized target "http://127.0.0.1:9" reason "unroutable docs fixture — nothing here ever runs"
